From: Andre Valentin <avalentin@marcant.net>
Subject: [PATCH] lua: declare the cmake minimum in the subproject too

lua/CMakeLists.txt is a complete PROJECT() of its own, but it inherited the
cmake_minimum_required() of the top level. That works while it is only ever
reached through ADD_SUBDIRECTORY; configuring it directly — which is what
building the lua binding alone amounts to — fails on cmake 4 with

  CMake Error in CMakeLists.txt: No cmake_minimum_required command is present.

Same version the top level asks for.

Signed-off-by: Andre Valentin <avalentin@marcant.net>
---
diff --git a/lua/CMakeLists.txt b/lua/CMakeLists.txt
index 0f9bf8f..9e74fb2 100644
--- a/lua/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/lua/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,3 +1,5 @@
+cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.13)
+
 PROJECT(ubus C)
 
 SET(CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX /)
